{"ticker":"ANDHRSUGAR","symbol":"ANDHRSUGAR","instrumentId":3097467,"name":"Andhra Sugars","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Specialty","about":"Andhra Sugars Ltd. is a diversified company engaged in the production of sugar, chemicals, and renewable energy. Its core operations include the manufacturing of high-quality sugar for domestic consumption and industrial use, along with the production of chemicals such as caustic soda, hydrogen peroxide, and chlorosulphonic acid, serving industries like pharmaceuticals, textiles, and agriculture. Additionally, Andhra Sugars generates renewable energy through co-generation power plants using bagasse, a byproduct of sugar production. The company focuses on sustainability and innovation, contributing to India's agro-industrial growth while ensuring environmentally friendly practices across its operations. Andhra Sugars is a trusted name in both domestic and international markets.","website":"www.theandhrasugars.com","location":"West Godavari, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:02:51.374Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":77.22,"changePct":0.1816294758692275,"week52High":103.95,"week52Low":67.05},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹1,047 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹2,526 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"67,767,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"62"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"4,186,011"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"1.30%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"0.63"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.7"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.02"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.08"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-23%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"10.89"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"8–52"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"5.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"9.43"},{"label":"Volume","value":"192,245"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"310,401"},{"label":"Master score","value":"38"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"